WEBVTT

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:33.450
To Sora:

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:39.300
Sorry about the other day.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.020
Don't be mad.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:47.650
Yagami Taichi.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.760
Writing an e-mail? {Oh, you're sending mail?} {mail kaiteru?}

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.850
D-Don't stare at me!

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.660
Huh? Are you going somewhere?

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.790
To a friend's birthday party. And this is the present.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.120
Gimme!

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:09.120
Nope.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:09.500
Gimme!

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:09.960
Nope.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:10.500
Gimme!

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.360
Nope.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:12.200
Stingy.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.950
To send mail, click here.

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.510
H-Hey!

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:16.710
Don't send it on your own!

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:18.740
Who is it for?

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.950
None of your business!

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:20.720
Meanie.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.220
I showed you how to send it...

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.450
Oh, you're going out?

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.220
Take care.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:29.300
Okay.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:32.110
Huh?

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.450
Mail rejected?

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.490
What's wrong with Sora?

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.940
She doesn't want to receive my mails, huh?

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.850
What is this...?

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.940
A... Digimon?

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.300
<b>gokigen na chou ni natte kirameku kaze ni notte</b>

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.300
I'll become a happy butterfly, and ride on the sparkling wind

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.850
<b>ima sugu kimi ni ai ni yukou</b>

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.850
I'm going to meet you right now

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.600
<b>yokei na koto nante wasureta hou ga mashi sa</b>

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.600
It's best to forget about things that don't matter

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:56.360
<b>kore ijou shareteru jikan wa nai</b>

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:56.360
There's no time to be fooling around

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:04.500
<b>nani ga wow wow wow wow wow kono sora ni todoku no darou</b>

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:04.500
I wonder wow wow wow wow wow, if we'll reach the sky

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.600
<b>dakedo wow wow wow wow wow</b>

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.600
Yet... wow wow wow wow wow

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.790
<b>ashita no yotei mo wakaranai</b>

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.790
I don't even know my plans for tomorrow

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:20.150
<b>mugendai na yume no ato no nanimo nai yo no naka ja</b>

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:20.150
After an infinite dream in an empty world

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:25.420
<b>sou sa itoshii omoi mo makesou ni naru kedo</b>

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:25.420
I feel like our precious memories will disappear

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:31.820
<b>stay shigachi na image darake no tayorinai tsubasa demo</b>

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:31.820
But even with those insecure wings full of images that tend to stay

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:40.180
<b>kitto toberu sa on my love</b>

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:40.180
I'm sure we can fly, on my love

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.100
Hey, isn't there anything to eat?

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.790
And Hikari gets to go to a birthday party and have cake...

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:01.650
I'll make you a cake.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.370
Really?

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.720
Yes, really. Can you get me some eggs?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.810
Let's see... did I forget the wheat flour?

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:11.270
Yo, Koshiro. Come in.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.310
Th-The egg...

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.440
The egg hatched!

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:19.620
No! A Digimon egg!

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.410
Oh, welcome, Koshiro-kun.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:23.820
Thank you.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:27.610
What's that thing? It looks like a jellyfish.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.590
It's a type of Digimon we've never seen before.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:30.830
It's kinda cute!

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:32.540
So what about it?

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:36.830
It seems like computer bugs from various places merged to form the egg.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.330
How do you know that?

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:45.020
A friend in Russia who I talk to a lot analyzed the data that forms the egg. {My net friend in L.A. decrypted the egg shell's data.}

00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:49.390
She's still in grade school, but she's already got a guaranteed opening at the university.{He's only in elementary school, but he also attends college.}

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:55.600
I'm in grade school too, and I only get to go to grade school.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:04:58.710
It evolved!

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:02.440
It's... an e-mail from the jellyfish.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.440
I'm hungry

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.610
I'm hungry

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.610
"I'm hungry..."

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:06.530
It's hungry?

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:10.670
This thing grows by eating data.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:12.380
And it's eating a lot...

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:19.080
It's only at Baby level now, but if it keeps evolving, it will eat data from all over the network.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.560
What happens when the data's eaten?

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:24.240
Computers will go haywire!

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:26.010
Are you serious!?

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.180
Welcome.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.730
That will be 125 yen.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:36.730
One, ten, hundred, thousand, ten thousand, hundred thousand...

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:39.470
That will be one million and 125 yen...

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:43.230
Welcome!

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.150
A million yen...

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.410
A million yen...

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.160
Why do I have to pay so much!?

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:01.380
<i>Supermarkets and convenience stores across the country are having trouble over issues in their computer systems.</i>

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.300
Taichi, I'm coming in. {unsubbed: "Excuse me!"}

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:05.350
Excuse me!

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:07.690
What's with the hurry?

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:08.590
We're gonna use Dad's computer!

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:10.780
Well, can you take these?

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:14.240
My, were you that thirsty?

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:15.100
Thank you!

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.000
Um... how did this work...

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.360
I'll do it.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.310
Please... I have no clue.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:23.450
Is this PC connected to a phone?

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:26.030
Y-Yeah. With ISDN or something.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:33.060
Hey, could we delete that jellyfish thing from the internet?

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.490
Delete? How?

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:40.170
If we told the phone company or a computer specialist...

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.170
That's useless.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.610
The friend in Russia I mentioned before told various people about it,

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:47.610
but they wouldn't listen to her{him}.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:50.670
It evolved again.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:53.250
It must be at Child level.

00:06:53.250 --> 00:06:54.760
This is bad...

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.010
This is bad, Koshiro!

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:57.810
Unless we defeat it now...

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:58.560
But how?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.430
Well...

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:02.810
Are we just gonna look while it keeps evolving?

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:12.260
If only Agumon was here now...

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:13.480
<i>Taichi...</i>

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:15.370
Agumon...

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.330
<i>Taichi!</i>

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.840
If only you were here...

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.880
<i>Taichi!</i>

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:21.780
Agumon? Is that you, Agumon?

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:23.280
Hey! Where are you, Agumon?

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:24.500
Taichi-san, here!

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:26.250
Agumon!

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:29.590
Taichi!

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.610
Agumon...

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:32.500
Gennai-san...

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.510
Long time no see.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:38.510
Koshiro-han, how've you been?

00:07:38.510 --> 00:07:39.660
Tentomon!

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.720
Piyomon! Gabumon! Palmon!

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.100
And everyone!

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:48.780
So, do you know about him?

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.700
Yes. A new type of Digimon in the net, right?

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:54.840
As expected from you.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:59.020
Be careful, Taichi. He's a really bad Digimon!

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.650
It will be really bad if we leave him be.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:04.570
Yeah... but how do we defeat him?

00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:08.480
Taichi... we'll fight.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:09.790
Agumon...

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:10.710
But—

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.750
We'll enter the net...

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:16.250
...and just like you all saved the Digital World...

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:19.390
...this is our turn to help you.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.740
Tentomon...

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:24.910
Got it. We're counting on you guys.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.670
You're the only ones who can do it.

00:08:26.670 --> 00:08:28.340
Koshiro, your Digivice?

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:30.430
I brought it, of course.

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:34.490
All right... we'll make you evolve with our Digivices!

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:36.250
OK!

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:40.750
Okay, I'll send Agumon and Tentomon to the net, so hold on a second.

00:08:40.750 --> 00:08:43.930
Okay, all set. I'll let everyone know!

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:47.530
Hello? This is Yagami, is Jou there?

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:50.340
Exams? {on-screen thingy: "Exam station - Shiba school central building, year 12 of the heisei era (2000)}

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.090
Exams... for middle school?

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:56.080
Okay, I understand.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:01.150
Yamato is out?

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:04.490
With Takeru? Um, where?

00:09:04.490 --> 00:09:05.690
Eh? Shimane?

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:07.110
Shimane...

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:10.570
Um, I'm sorry, is there a phone number where I can contact them?

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:09.300
Koshiro-kun, would you like some Oolong tea?

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.570
Ah, sure.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:14.890
Answer answer answer answer answer...

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:13.990
Here you go.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.240
Thank you.

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:16.070
Hello?

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:18.700
May I ask who is speaking?

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.720
<i>I'm Yagami, from Tokyo...</i>

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:22.120
<i>E-Excuse me, um...</i>

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.280
Sorry, could you please repeat that?

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:29.410
<i>Um... can I speak to Yamato and Takeru, please?</i>

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:32.970
Yes, they're my grandchildren. They're really good boys...

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.490
Who is it?

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:35.560
<i>Excuse me, there's something important I have to tell them!</i>

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:37.090
I see.

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:38.460
Yamato...

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.480
She hung up...

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.710
Are you going somewhere for spring break, Koshiro-kun?

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.210
Oh well, next!

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:49.930
No, not really.

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:52.320
Don't you feel like going somewhere?

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:52.980
Ah, hello?

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:56.030
<i>This is Mimi! Please leave a message!</i>

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:57.620
<i>Mimi-chan!</i>

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:00.990
<i>Ah, I'm Taichi. Call me right away, okay?</i>

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.230
Man, all of them...

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:06.080
Sorry for making you help out.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:09.540
Hey, do you know the number of the house Hikari went to?

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.250
Like this?

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:14.720
Yes, make sure it doesn't get lumpy. {seems to be something like 'make sure it doesn't get any balls, but ehh}

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.720
C'mon, Mom!

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:17.040
Right, right... there's a memo right there.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:19.020
Uri-san's house.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:20.540
Seriously...

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:22.960
Happy Birthday!

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.230
Hikari-chan...

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:34.820
I can't go home yet. We still haven't even blown out the candles...

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:38.240
Okay then, come home after you blow out the candles.

00:10:39.090 --> 00:10:40.180
Koshiro!

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:44.540
S-Say... can you call Sora's home for me?

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.250
Sora-san? Shouldn't you do it?

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.900
Just do it. Here!

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:52.930
Oh, you're calling more friends over?

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:54.550
Gimme some Oolong tea too.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.960
Why don't you answer me?

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:01.930
Okay, I just have to let her know to call the Yagami residence, right?

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:04.490
One moment, she just came home.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:05.950
<i>Who is it?</i>

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:07.570
<i>It's from the Yagami residence.</i>

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:09.590
<i>Say I'm not home.</i>

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:10.230
<i>But...</i>

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:11.390
<i>Just do it.</i>

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:13.030
Um...

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.320
She told me to say she's not home...

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:19.020
Did something happen?

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:19.990
Not really.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.340
Something happened, right?

00:11:21.340 --> 00:11:22.720
It's nothing...

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:25.410
This isn't the time to be worrying about fights!

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:26.950
It's not that!

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:28.340
So it <i>is</i> a fight...

00:11:28.340 --> 00:11:31.340
A-Anyway, isn't it about time now?

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.160
Taichi, you jerk.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:42.260
This is scary...

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.220
This is lame...

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:45.000
No kidding.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:49.020
Huh? Isn't it going faster?

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:52.030
I'm scared!

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:55.740
Taichi?

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:59.110
The ferris wheel is really going around today...

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:03.920
Transfer complete.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.410
Agumon!

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:11.750
Taichi! Koshiro! We're here!

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.440
I'm counting on you, Agumon!

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:15.460
Tentomon, we have a preemptive strike!

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.820
He doesn't know we're here yet!

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:27.280
Shall we do it?

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:39.650
All right!

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:44.900
Let's play?

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:46.990
What do you mean, "let's play"?

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:49.670
Hurry up and beat that thing!

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:51.410
Tentomon, evolve!

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:52.410
Right!

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.750
Tentomon, evolve!

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.750
Agumon, evolve!

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.870
Kabuterimon!

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:02.870
Greymon!

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:23.840
Good!

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:26.030
That thing's pretty weak!

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:26.740
Hold on.

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:38.880
He... evolved!

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:42.800
Don't worry. He's only at Adult level, like ours.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:03.360
Did we get him?

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:17.910
We can't hurt him! What's going on here?

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.170
Kabuterimon!

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:26.720
Greymon!

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:28.720
Taichi-san, I got it!

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.300
He's... at Perfect level.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.950
Then, just now...

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:34.350
It was a two-level evolution.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:35.460
Not good...

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:37.350
Evolve to Perfect level as well!

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:50.910
He's attacking during evolution...

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:06.660
Are you okay, Agumon?

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:08.430
Sorry, Taichi...

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:09.620
Tentomon...

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:12.290
That guy's unbelievable...

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:20.510
We'll have to let them rest for a bit.

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:24.860
Damn! Attacking while they're evolving, that's dirty!

00:15:24.860 --> 00:15:28.780
Taichi-san, we got an e-mail from a guy in Australia.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.740
He says it's the first time he's seen a Digital Monster. {on-screen email: "Those monsters just now were Digital Monsters? I've never seen one of those. - Toma"} {sakki no digital monster to iu n desu ka? hajimete mimashita. // toma"}

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:33.770
Those monsters just now were

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:33.770
Digital Monsters?

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:33.770
I've never seen one of those.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:33.770
Toma

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:34.000
He was watching that fight?

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.070
This one is from Singapore.

00:15:34.570 --> 00:15:39.540
Jane

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:38.630
"It was two on one and you lost, are you that weak?" {email <- that, signed Jane}

00:15:38.630 --> 00:15:39.580
Shut up!

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.440
And there's a few more.

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.730
An e-mail from the jellyfish...

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.060
"Hello hello hello hello..."?

00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:46.960
What's that about?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.500
We're in big trouble!

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:50.350
Look at the address!

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:53.010
He's in the NTT system!

00:15:53.670 --> 00:15:55.210
NTT?

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:57.140
We have to contact everyone now!

00:16:01.280 --> 00:16:02.570
Did you draw the Joker?

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:04.630
Don't hide it, Noriko-chan.

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:12.280
Hikari-chan...

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:13.640
I can't...

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:16.520
I can't just leave when I'm the one who's winning.

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:19.840
Forget the game and just come home!

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:21.400
Next...

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:26.530
Busy signal? Damn...

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:30.960
Busy again...

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:34.800
At Jou's place too...

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:39.430
Y... Yamato's too?

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:41.320
It's busy everywhere!

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:42.330
What about Sora-san's?

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:44.170
But we already called there...

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:46.230
Hello?

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:50.650
Hello-hello-hello-hello-hello...

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:52.230
N-Not good...

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:04.750
What's going on?

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:08.390
He entered the phone switch server and is jamming the lines. {He's hacked the phone switches and is repeatedly calling all the phone numbers.}

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:10.150
He's trying to bring the system down.

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:11.370
This is bad...

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:15.920
If the phones don't work, we can't contact the others and the internet will also...

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:20.240
It disconnected...

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:27.480
<i>Now for some breaking news...</i>

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:31.370
<i>Currently in Tokyo, the phone system is experiencing difficulties.</i>

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:33.200
Lots of things are happening today...

00:17:31.370 --> 00:17:35.180
<i>According to NTT, this is due to heavy phone traffic,</i> {they have 'The phone company closed the lines for maintenance.'}

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:35.450
Oh? Koshiro-kun, you're leaving already?

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:41.290
<i>and some areas have stopped working due to the call volume.</i>

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.960
I'll be back soon!

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:40.410
Mom...

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:42.010
What's wrong, Taichi?

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:46.660
<i>Currently, technicians are working to restore the downed switches,</i>

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:43.580
It's all over...

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.120
What are you talking about?

00:17:46.660 --> 00:17:51.840
<i>and are urging consumers to to refrain from using the phone or cell phone services.</i>

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.130
That feels good...

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:56.130
That Taichi... what did he want?

00:18:00.140 --> 00:18:03.660
<i>However, if there is a necessity to get in touch with somebody, </i>

00:18:04.050 --> 00:18:08.640
<i>we recommend using the emergency voice mail system by dialing 171.</i>

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:14.600
<i>With the emergency voice mail system, your message will be stored even when the system is down or busy.</i>

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:16.640
<i>It was created in 1995...</i>

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.640
Th... that's it!

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.510
<i>This is the emergency voice mail system.</i>

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:23.520
<i>To record a message, press one.</i>

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.450
Hello? Yamato?

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:29.540
When you hear this, give me a reply. It's important!

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:33.530
Jou, when you hear this, give me a reply.

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:37.540
Hikari? I told you to come home!

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:41.360
Sora, I'll apologize for the other day.

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:45.470
So, when you hear this, give me a reply!

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.480
Taichi, you jerk.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:58.070
Mimi-chan, when you hear this, please give me a call.

00:18:58.070 --> 00:18:59.820
Oh, I forgot...

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:00.730
What?

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:02.940
We got a postcard from Mimi-chan.

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:06.240
Mimi-chan? Wh-where is she?

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:08.750
Hawaii...

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:15.600
Hawaii is so nice!

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:21.880
Oh, welcome.

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:22.870
Thank you.

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:25.750
What's wrong, Taichi-san?

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:29.410
Hawaii, huh?

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:31.760
We're totally done for.

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:35.170
It's getting tough to gather everyone, huh? {I guess we're not that tight of a group anymore.}

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:36.900
By the way, where did you go?

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:39.540
This is a satellite cell phone.

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:40.490
Satellite?

00:19:41.190 --> 00:19:44.150
With this, we don't have to go through an NTT switch,

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:46.200
and we can connect directly to a foreign access point.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:48.920
So if we use it to call Yamato and the others...

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:50.110
That's not possible.

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:52.670
Local calls still go through the switches.

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:55.040
What the hell, man...

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:58.110
Why don't we check if there are any messages in the 171 system?

00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:59.450
Right, I forgot.

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:02.070
<i>Playing back message.</i>

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:05.580
<i>Hello? This is Yamato.</i>

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:07.570
<i>What was so urgent?</i>

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:09.570
All right!

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:11.390
I knew we could count on them.

00:20:14.170 --> 00:20:16.240
<i>Do you two have your Digivices?</i>

00:20:16.240 --> 00:20:16.900
Koshiro?

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:19.200
<i>We have them.</i>

00:20:19.200 --> 00:20:20.910
<i>Hey, what's going on?</i>

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:24.920
<i>Get to a PC, quickly.</i>

00:20:24.920 --> 00:20:27.770
<i>A new type of Digimon showed up in the net.</i>

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:30.340
<i>We need you to help us fight him again!</i>

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:31.410
That's bad...

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:39.090
<i>Well... we have our Digivices, but this is Grandma's house, so we don't have a PC...</i>

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:43.060
<i>There may not be any around... this is Shimane after all.</i>

00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:48.520
We're totally done for!

00:20:48.520 --> 00:20:52.060
Please! Try to find a PC somehow!

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:54.660
<i>There has to be a PC somewhere in Shimane!</i>

00:20:55.050 --> 00:20:56.630
Hurry, Takeru!

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.450
Okay, it connected!

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:02.090
Good job, satellite cell phone!

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.900
Huh? He's not there.

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:06.540
Did he get out of the NTT?

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:07.370
Hey...

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:09.360
Found him!

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:09.360
Not here! Not here! Boo!

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:10.370
Not here! Not here! Boo!

00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:11.620
He's... in America!

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:13.120
America?

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:14.330
A PC?

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:16.820
I have one but it's broken right now.

00:21:16.820 --> 00:21:20.830
A PC? We don't have anything like that!

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:24.370
A P what...?

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:26.830
A P what?

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:30.970
There's no way we're gonna find a PC in Shimane!

00:21:32.220 --> 00:21:33.710
There!

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:38.600
Sorry, but that computer isn't hooked up to the internet.

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:41.530
C'mon, just let them use it.

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:43.350
Sho-chan, don't you have deliveries to do?

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:44.700
I feel sorry for them.

00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:46.920
But it's not hooked up to the internet!

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:48.510
Then hook it up!

00:21:48.510 --> 00:21:49.270
Sho-chan, you...

00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:50.320
Hey, hey, you two!

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:53.910
Where are we going?

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:55.000
Leave it to me!

00:22:21.250 --> 00:22:24.430
Stupid thing... he's having fun!

00:22:24.430 --> 00:22:28.140
Even at Perfect level, he's still a newborn.

00:22:28.140 --> 00:22:29.810
Who knows what it would do?

00:22:30.140 --> 00:22:33.040
Can't anyone stop him somehow?

00:22:33.040 --> 00:22:37.120
There will be adults who will realize they're not dealing with an ordinary computer issue.

00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:40.750
But they'd have no idea that a Digimon is causing it.

00:22:41.410 --> 00:22:44.070
So... what do we do?

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:47.000
All we can do is let Agumon and the rest fight him...

00:22:47.000 --> 00:22:49.380
But even then...

00:22:49.750 --> 00:22:50.380
Yamato!

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:51.290
<i>Sorry to keep you waiting.</i>

00:22:51.290 --> 00:22:53.330
<i>We've got our Digivices!</i>

00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:55.040
<i>I see... that's good.</i>

00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:56.970
<i>So you found a PC?</i>

00:22:57.890 --> 00:22:58.890
Yeah, well...

00:22:59.370 --> 00:23:02.460
Can we really let those kids use it?

00:23:02.460 --> 00:23:04.460
Stop complaining and let them use it!

00:23:04.460 --> 00:23:06.310
They're Kinu-san's grandkids.

00:23:06.310 --> 00:23:08.910
Life in Tokyo sure is different. {Tokyo kids sure are trendy.}

00:23:08.910 --> 00:23:11.130
Hey! What's wrong, Yamato?

00:23:11.130 --> 00:23:12.110
Hey!

00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:16.330
N-No... it's nothing.

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:19.630
I was worried for a while there.

00:23:20.630 --> 00:23:23.310
Taichi-san, can I have your Oolong tea?

00:23:23.310 --> 00:23:25.850
Aren't you drinking too much?

00:23:27.940 --> 00:23:30.350
Aren't the others connected yet?

00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:33.710
If not, it's up to us two to fight him again.

00:23:33.710 --> 00:23:34.810
Yeah, but...

00:23:34.810 --> 00:23:36.100
Agumon! Tentomon!

00:23:38.250 --> 00:23:40.060
Gabumon and Patamon!

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:41.670
We're here too!

00:23:41.670 --> 00:23:42.480
Sorry we're late!

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:44.050
We're counting on you, Gabumon!

00:23:44.050 --> 00:23:46.170
Good luck, Patamon!

00:23:46.170 --> 00:23:48.270
I'll guide you to him, guys.

00:23:48.270 --> 00:23:49.290
OK!

00:23:49.290 --> 00:23:52.240
This time we <i>will</i> beat him!

00:24:00.450 --> 00:24:03.120
Sign: "Over here"

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:04.620
He's messing with us...

00:24:04.620 --> 00:24:06.590
Yamato, here we go!

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:08.080
Straight to Ultimate!

00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:12.970
Agumon, warp-evolve!

00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:12.970
Gabumon, warp-evolve!

00:24:32.610 --> 00:24:35.450
WarGreymon!

00:24:36.050 --> 00:24:38.410
MetalGarurumon!

00:24:39.950 --> 00:24:45.750
<b>nigetari akirameru koto wa daremo</b>

00:24:39.950 --> 00:24:45.750
Given time, anyone can give up and run

00:24:46.670 --> 00:24:52.630
<b>isshun areba dekiru kara arukitsuzukeyou</b>

00:24:46.670 --> 00:24:52.630
So just keep on walking instead

00:24:49.410 --> 00:24:50.300
Nice!

00:24:50.300 --> 00:24:52.210
Patamon, you evolve too!

00:24:52.630 --> 00:24:58.030
<b>kimi ni shika dekinai koto ga aru</b>

00:24:52.630 --> 00:24:58.030
There's something only you can do

00:24:53.000 --> 00:24:55.530
Patamon, evolve!

00:24:58.030 --> 00:25:06.560
<b>aoi hoshi ni hikari ga nakusenu you ni</b>

00:24:58.030 --> 00:25:06.560
so the light of this blue Earth doesn't fade away

00:25:00.690 --> 00:25:02.280
He evolved!?

00:25:02.280 --> 00:25:03.310
He's fast!

00:25:05.910 --> 00:25:07.150
Patamon!

00:25:08.270 --> 00:25:09.440
Patamon!

00:25:11.360 --> 00:25:13.810
Patamon! Are you okay!?

00:25:13.810 --> 00:25:14.910
Tentomon!

00:25:14.910 --> 00:25:16.820
I'm okay... but Patamon...

00:25:17.130 --> 00:25:20.670
Patamon! I'll be right there!

00:25:20.670 --> 00:25:21.930
Patamon!

00:25:21.930 --> 00:25:23.950
Patamon! Patamon!

00:25:23.950 --> 00:25:25.090
How dare you...

00:25:25.090 --> 00:25:26.970
How dare you do that to Patamon!?

00:25:26.970 --> 00:25:28.370
You're gonna pay!

00:25:31.390 --> 00:25:34.390
<b>hashire! kaze yori hayaku</b>

00:25:31.390 --> 00:25:34.390
Run faster than the wind

00:25:34.390 --> 00:25:38.510
<b>mezase! sora yori tooku</b>

00:25:34.390 --> 00:25:38.510
Aim beyond the sky

00:25:38.510 --> 00:25:44.560
<b>atarashii jibun ni aeru sa</b>

00:25:38.510 --> 00:25:44.560
You can meet a new "you"

00:25:44.560 --> 00:25:51.440
<b>shiranai yuuki ga nemuru heart ni ki ga tsuitara</b>

00:25:44.560 --> 00:25:51.440
Once you notice the unknown courage sleeping in your heart

00:25:44.940 --> 00:25:47.350
Tentomon, take care of Patamon!

00:25:47.350 --> 00:25:49.060
WarGreymon, keep attacking!

00:25:51.440 --> 00:25:53.480
T-Taichi-san...

00:25:51.440 --> 00:25:58.980
<b>mune no naka no doshaburi mo kitto yamu kara</b>

00:25:51.440 --> 00:25:58.980
the downpour in your heart's sure to stop

00:25:53.480 --> 00:25:54.910
Good, keep going!

00:25:54.910 --> 00:25:57.950
Ta... Taichi-san...

00:25:57.950 --> 00:25:58.950
There! Go!

00:25:58.950 --> 00:25:59.820
All right!

00:25:58.980 --> 00:26:01.370
<b>Show me your brave heart</b>

00:25:59.820 --> 00:26:00.830
Taichi-san!

00:26:00.830 --> 00:26:02.140
What?

00:26:02.140 --> 00:26:03.590
I can't hold it...

00:26:03.590 --> 00:26:04.490
Hold what?

00:26:04.490 --> 00:26:07.960
I have to go to the toilet...

00:26:08.550 --> 00:26:12.130
Hey... why now, of all times?

00:26:12.130 --> 00:26:13.000
Hey!

00:26:13.880 --> 00:26:15.610
Okay, finish him off!

00:26:17.680 --> 00:26:19.490
Please hit!

00:26:21.120 --> 00:26:22.280
Damn it!

00:26:24.220 --> 00:26:27.480
What's wrong, Taichi? WarGreymon stopped moving!

00:26:31.090 --> 00:26:32.760
Sorry about that.

00:26:32.760 --> 00:26:34.690
It's not working!

00:26:34.690 --> 00:26:36.250
What have you done!?

00:26:36.810 --> 00:26:38.250
I didn't do anything!

00:26:38.250 --> 00:26:40.410
It's your fault for going to the toilet at a time like this!

00:26:40.410 --> 00:26:41.910
No good...

00:26:41.910 --> 00:26:44.290
Why did you freeze the system?

00:26:44.290 --> 00:26:46.880
I didn't do it on purpose!

00:26:46.880 --> 00:26:49.040
This is why you and Sora-san get into fights!

00:26:49.040 --> 00:26:50.400
I just...

00:26:51.360 --> 00:26:54.030
I only... got her a present.

00:26:54.520 --> 00:26:55.300
A present?

00:26:57.100 --> 00:27:01.740
It was her birthday, so I gave her a hairclip.

00:27:01.740 --> 00:27:08.220
But then she goes "So this hat doesn't suit me?"... and we got into a fight.

00:27:08.220 --> 00:27:09.720
Just that...

00:27:09.720 --> 00:27:13.310
But I apologized!

00:27:14.690 --> 00:27:16.350
It's back to normal!

00:27:17.360 --> 00:27:18.650
WarGreymon!

00:27:19.860 --> 00:27:22.070
Taichi! Koshiro!

00:27:22.070 --> 00:27:24.580
What were you doing, you morons!?

00:27:25.440 --> 00:27:30.210
WarGreymon!

00:27:30.210 --> 00:27:32.780
WarGreymon!!

00:27:33.370 --> 00:27:36.210
Ta... Taichi...

00:27:39.030 --> 00:27:40.590
If I...

00:27:40.590 --> 00:27:42.590
If I had been there, this wouldn't have...

00:27:42.590 --> 00:27:43.720
"You lost again?"

00:27:43.720 --> 00:27:44.220
What?

00:27:44.220 --> 00:27:46.180
That was from Canberra.

00:27:46.180 --> 00:27:48.900
"You almost won, what were you doing?"

00:27:48.900 --> 00:27:50.400
That's from Berlin—

00:27:50.400 --> 00:27:52.470
What's wrong with you, jackass?

00:27:52.470 --> 00:27:54.620
I was just reading the mails that came in!

00:27:54.620 --> 00:27:56.910
Koshiro, you...

00:27:56.910 --> 00:28:00.200
Cut it out! This is no time for fights!

00:28:02.860 --> 00:28:04.700
Stupid mail!

00:28:18.800 --> 00:28:25.180
"Who has the clock?"

00:28:25.840 --> 00:28:27.260
Clock...?

00:28:31.100 --> 00:28:32.180
He's copying himself...

00:28:35.190 --> 00:28:36.940
These numbers...

00:28:38.850 --> 00:28:39.940
Now what?

00:28:41.420 --> 00:28:45.400
A middle school student in Taiwan who hacked into the Pentagon just told me...

00:28:45.400 --> 00:28:50.290
30 minutes ago, a nuclear missile was launched from an American military base.

00:28:51.510 --> 00:28:54.120
There was a bug in the launch computer...

00:28:54.120 --> 00:28:56.430
Of course, it's all his doing!

00:28:56.430 --> 00:28:58.210
Then, this number is...

00:28:58.210 --> 00:29:02.230
Probably, the time remaining until the missile hits the target.

00:29:04.720 --> 00:29:07.360
Y-You're kidding me, right?

00:29:07.360 --> 00:29:11.870
There's one missile, codename Peace Keeper.

00:29:11.870 --> 00:29:15.190
Range of 20,000 kilometers, that's pretty much the entire Earth.

00:29:15.190 --> 00:29:17.730
Max speed of 15,000 miles per hour.

00:29:18.100 --> 00:29:20.690
Um, what's that in kilometers?

00:29:20.690 --> 00:29:23.700
Parentheses, Mach 23.

00:29:23.700 --> 00:29:25.740
T... twenty three...

00:29:26.310 --> 00:29:31.240
But we don't know what the target is, or where the missile is now.

00:29:31.240 --> 00:29:34.560
It's just going to explode somewhere in the world...

00:29:34.560 --> 00:29:36.380
In nine minutes.

00:29:36.700 --> 00:29:38.220
It's getting cloudy.

00:29:38.220 --> 00:29:43.030
You're right. I should go bring in the laundry right away.

00:29:43.030 --> 00:29:43.880
Right away.

00:29:44.240 --> 00:29:49.450
Would you bring this to Kinu-san? Tell her it's from Yasuko.

00:29:52.470 --> 00:29:54.480
Are you listening?

00:29:54.920 --> 00:29:57.220
A mail from Indonesia.

00:29:57.220 --> 00:29:59.040
"Please defeat the enemy."

00:29:59.040 --> 00:30:00.940
This one is from Armenia.

00:30:00.940 --> 00:30:03.300
"You're the only ones who can defeat that monster."

00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:05.610
From Qatar: "Please do your best."

00:30:06.420 --> 00:30:07.490
"Do your best..."

00:30:08.350 --> 00:30:10.860
But we can't defeat all of them!

00:30:10.860 --> 00:30:14.660
The missile won't explode as long as the fuse doesn't activate.

00:30:14.660 --> 00:30:18.630
If this is a game, only one of them will have the clock.

00:30:18.630 --> 00:30:21.540
If we defeat that one, the fuse shouldn't activate.

00:30:21.540 --> 00:30:24.160
But how are we going to find that one?

00:30:24.160 --> 00:30:27.370
Well... all we can do is defeat them one by one.

00:30:27.370 --> 00:30:29.550
That would take too long!

00:30:34.160 --> 00:30:36.560
But it's the only way.

00:30:38.630 --> 00:30:39.700
Taichi...

00:30:41.030 --> 00:30:42.610
Taichi...

00:30:42.980 --> 00:30:44.150
Taichi!

00:30:44.520 --> 00:30:48.170
Taichi, be strong, and leave it to us.

00:30:48.170 --> 00:30:49.740
WarGreymon...

00:30:50.150 --> 00:30:52.760
Do you know where he is?

00:30:52.760 --> 00:30:54.330
MetalGarurumon...

00:30:54.330 --> 00:30:55.780
Everyone...

00:30:56.660 --> 00:30:58.970
I'll send you the address now!

00:30:58.970 --> 00:30:59.970
Please.

00:31:04.070 --> 00:31:06.890
Right... it's the only way...

00:31:08.050 --> 00:31:09.470
Sorry.

00:31:09.470 --> 00:31:10.330
It's fine.

00:31:11.780 --> 00:31:14.850
Seven minutes left.

00:31:14.850 --> 00:31:16.170
Oh no!

00:31:37.230 --> 00:31:39.260
So much mail...

00:31:40.160 --> 00:31:43.540
"Good luck, WarGreymon," from Costa Rica.

00:31:43.540 --> 00:31:46.930
"Don't lose, MetalGarurumon," from the Philippines.

00:31:46.930 --> 00:31:48.260
They keep coming in!

00:31:48.600 --> 00:31:51.760
Big brother... don't give up.

00:31:52.830 --> 00:31:55.760
I won't give up... not until it's over.

00:31:56.710 --> 00:31:59.770
There's no way... I'm giving up.

00:32:22.060 --> 00:32:24.640
How many are there?

00:32:24.640 --> 00:32:26.650
4,000... 8,000...

00:32:26.650 --> 00:32:29.170
He copied himself again! 16,000...

00:32:29.170 --> 00:32:30.410
He keeps copying himself!

00:32:47.290 --> 00:32:48.960
MetalGarurumon!

00:32:51.680 --> 00:32:53.990
Their movement's weird!

00:32:53.990 --> 00:32:56.160
It's because of the mail from all over the world!

00:32:56.480 --> 00:32:59.410
It's slowing down our processing speed!

00:32:59.690 --> 00:33:01.950
<i>They're getting hit really bad!</i>

00:33:01.950 --> 00:33:05.860
Everyone around the world, WarGreymon and
MetalGarurumon's response time is increasing!

00:33:06.270 --> 00:33:08.470
Stop sending mails, please!

00:33:21.450 --> 00:33:23.160
WarGreymon!

00:33:48.570 --> 00:33:51.060
Koshiro-kun, will you have lunch with us?

00:33:51.930 --> 00:33:54.590
No good... the mails won't stopping...

00:33:54.590 --> 00:33:56.870
Less than five minutes left... now what?

00:33:56.870 --> 00:33:59.170
Looks like I'm in the way...

00:33:59.170 --> 00:34:02.100
Huh? Where did Taichi go?

00:34:14.900 --> 00:34:16.320
WarGreymon!

00:34:22.280 --> 00:34:23.610
Metal...

00:34:24.170 --> 00:34:26.300
MetalGarurumon!

00:34:27.050 --> 00:34:30.930
It's me, Yamato. Can you hear me?

00:34:30.930 --> 00:34:32.290
Open your eyes!

00:34:32.630 --> 00:34:34.040
Yamato...

00:34:36.520 --> 00:34:39.100
I'm here! I'm here too!

00:34:39.100 --> 00:34:41.300
To fight together!

00:34:41.860 --> 00:34:45.660
I... I won't let you fight alone.

00:34:46.780 --> 00:34:48.600
I'll be here with you.

00:34:48.600 --> 00:34:50.840
I'm with you, WarGreymon!

00:35:34.550 --> 00:35:37.390
Hey, where'd your brother go?

00:35:38.260 --> 00:35:39.740
Here...

00:35:49.890 --> 00:35:51.250
WarGreymon and...

00:35:51.580 --> 00:35:53.270
...MetalGarurumon...

00:35:53.680 --> 00:35:55.210
...combined!

00:36:12.300 --> 00:36:13.080
Amazing!

00:36:50.420 --> 00:36:53.680
Th-There he is! That's the final one!

00:36:53.680 --> 00:36:56.230
The one with the clock!

00:37:02.120 --> 00:37:02.940
Can't find him!

00:37:03.700 --> 00:37:05.570
We have one minute!

00:37:05.570 --> 00:37:06.670
One minute left!

00:37:06.670 --> 00:37:07.770
One minute left.

00:37:18.240 --> 00:37:19.650
Big brother!

00:37:19.650 --> 00:37:23.800
Hurry up and find him! There's no time left!

00:37:23.800 --> 00:37:25.810
Big brother! Hurry!

00:37:25.810 --> 00:37:28.010
<i>He's got too much speed...</i>

00:37:28.010 --> 00:37:31.610
<i>Even if we have more power, our response time's hampering us.</i>

00:37:31.610 --> 00:37:32.840
<i>What can we do?</i>

00:37:33.600 --> 00:37:34.770
30 seconds left!

00:37:36.270 --> 00:37:38.560
That's it... I can redirect them!

00:37:38.560 --> 00:37:42.570
If I redirect all this mail to his address...!

00:37:44.360 --> 00:37:46.740
Go!

00:38:06.990 --> 00:38:08.560
Ten seconds left!

00:38:08.560 --> 00:38:09.550
Nine!

00:38:09.550 --> 00:38:10.540
Eight!

00:38:10.540 --> 00:38:11.550
Seven!

00:38:11.550 --> 00:38:12.350
Six!

00:38:12.350 --> 00:38:13.390
Five!

00:38:13.390 --> 00:38:14.390
Four!

00:38:14.390 --> 00:38:15.390
Three!

00:38:15.390 --> 00:38:16.380
Two!

00:38:16.380 --> 00:38:17.230
One!

00:38:25.140 --> 00:38:26.700
It's ruined...

00:38:26.700 --> 00:38:30.400
That's weird, it's all computer-controlled...

00:38:41.040 --> 00:38:42.420
To Sora:

00:38:41.040 --> 00:38:42.420
Sorry about the

00:38:41.040 --> 00:38:42.420
other day.

00:38:41.040 --> 00:38:42.420
Don't be mad.

00:38:45.770 --> 00:38:47.450
We didn't make it...

00:39:01.440 --> 00:39:03.910
Taichi, you dummy...

00:39:06.830 --> 00:39:10.620
We... we... we...

00:39:10.620 --> 00:39:12.450
We made it...

00:39:19.660 --> 00:39:27.170
<b>hirogaru sora nagame hotto hitoiki tsuita</b>

00:39:19.660 --> 00:39:27.170
<b>I take a deep breath under the view of the spreading sky</b>

00:39:27.170 --> 00:39:34.470
<b>time capsule ni wa omoide tsumekonda yo</b>

00:39:27.170 --> 00:39:34.470
<b>Wrapping my memories in a time capsule</b>

00:39:34.600 --> 00:39:41.810
<b>papa to mama ni wa himitsu ni shite dekakeyou</b>

00:39:34.600 --> 00:39:41.810
<b>Let's go out without telling Mom and Dad</b>

00:39:41.940 --> 00:39:48.530
<b>boku ni wa minna no chikara ga tsuiteru</b>

00:39:41.940 --> 00:39:48.530
<b>I have everybody's strength with me</b>

00:40:05.680 --> 00:40:11.970
<b>yukou mirai no boukensha</b>

00:40:05.680 --> 00:40:11.970
<b>Let's go! Future adventurers</b>

00:40:13.130 --> 00:40:19.350
<b>sagasou tsutsumu hikari-tachi o</b>

00:40:13.130 --> 00:40:19.350
<b>Searching for the light enveloping us!</b>

00:40:20.770 --> 00:40:28.110
<b>ashita ni wa ikutsumo no yume ga matte iru no sa</b>

00:40:20.770 --> 00:40:28.110
<b>Many dreams await us tomorrow</b>

00:40:28.110 --> 00:40:38.580
<b>ima yori mo tsuyoku nareru yo ne bokura wa kitto</b>

00:40:28.110 --> 00:40:38.580
<b>And that way I know we'll become stronger</b>

00:40:28.690 --> 00:40:28.980
Taichi, I'm sorry.

00:40:28.980 --> 00:40:29.230
Taichi, I'm sorry.

00:40:29.230 --> 00:40:29.440
Taichi, I'm sorry.

00:40:29.440 --> 00:40:29.730
Taichi, I'm sorry.

00:40:29.730 --> 00:40:30.150
Taichi, I'm sorry.

00:40:30.150 --> 00:40:30.440
Taichi, I'm sorry.

00:40:30.440 --> 00:40:30.690
Taichi, I'm sorry.

00:40:30.690 --> 00:40:30.940
Taichi, I'm sorry.

00:40:30.940 --> 00:40:35.700
Taichi, I'm sorry.

00:40:31.490 --> 00:40:31.690
Thanks for

00:40:31.690 --> 00:40:31.950
Thanks for

00:40:31.950 --> 00:40:32.200
Thanks for

00:40:32.200 --> 00:40:32.450
Thanks for

00:40:32.450 --> 00:40:35.700
Thanks for

00:40:32.740 --> 00:40:32.990
the present.

